            <div xml:id="d214">

                <pb facs="0346" n="247" sameAs="frus:frus1936v05/pg247"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">632.6231/42a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Gibson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-04-17T18:00:00-05:00">April 17, 1936—6 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>62. Please comment briefly by cable on story in today’s issue of <hi
                        rendition="#italic">New York Times</hi> that the Brazilian Foreign Trade
                    Council has recommended “an emergency commercial agreement (with Germany) as a
                    method of selling surplus cotton stocks Germany is willing to buy with
                    compensated marks.”</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
